                <pb facs="0632" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123J634/345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-09T17:00:00+08:00">June 9, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 9—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. Having approached Foreign Office with view to obtaining <hi
                        rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> of Chinese Government to appointment of
                    Minister Johnson as Ambassador to China, Director of the Department of
                    International Affairs of Foreign Office informs me that his Government will
                    receive Mr. Johnson as Ambassador with great pleasure.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
